1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,521
OneNMRD Interface controls NMR
relaxometry experiments and

2
00:00:05,521 --> 00:00:08,231
analyses their NMRD profiles.

3
00:00:08,481 --> 00:00:11,858
It works with conventional and
fast-field-cycling consoles,

4
00:00:11,858 --> 00:00:13,352
in your web browser.

5
00:00:13,602 --> 00:00:18,111
Everything in this tour comes from its
built-in simulator: no hardware is moved.

6
00:00:19,761 --> 00:00:23,586
One interface drives different
consoles and magnets.

7
00:00:23,836 --> 00:00:27,820
FFC4, the fast-field-cycling
relaxometer at IST,

8
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:31,740
runs on a Magritek Kea
console with Prospa.

9
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:35,887
The Resonance Systems
ultraRelax8 runs through uSpin32,

10
00:00:35,887 --> 00:00:39,779
with generated run scripts
and its exported scans.

11
00:00:40,029 --> 00:00:43,863
The fixed-field setup uses
its compatible magnet. The

12
00:00:43,863 --> 00:00:46,395
simulator stands in for each setup,

13
00:00:46,395 --> 00:00:48,553
for training and testing.

14
00:00:50,203 --> 00:00:54,632
Choose a complete setup
at the top: FFC plus Kea,

15
00:00:54,632 --> 00:00:59,140
FFC plus uSpin32, or
Fixed field plus uSpin32.

16
00:00:59,390 --> 00:01:03,358
On the ultraRelax8, the
field-cycling device levels,

17
00:01:03,358 --> 00:01:06,639
V1 and V2, come from
the field calibration,

18
00:01:06,639 --> 00:01:09,050
within the firmware limits.

19
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:14,382
The sequences are field-cycling
and standard ones.

20
00:01:14,632 --> 00:01:16,606
Eight field-cycling sequences:

21
00:01:16,606 --> 00:01:20,094
polarised at high field or
starting from a low field,

22
00:01:20,094 --> 00:01:24,260
with inversion or saturation,
each also with a solid echo.

23
00:01:24,510 --> 00:01:29,609
Inversion recovery and saturation
recovery are the standard T1 sequences,

24
00:01:29,609 --> 00:01:32,404
at fixed field, on the ultraRelax8.

25
00:01:32,654 --> 00:01:36,935
RF tuning, and a Tune of any
sequence, come before the run.

26
00:01:38,585 --> 00:01:41,900
Each timing diagram is drawn
from the sequence definition in

27
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:43,060
the console settings,

28
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:44,957
with the current parameters.

29
00:01:45,207 --> 00:01:47,083
It shows the field switching,

30
00:01:47,083 --> 00:01:49,283
the RF pulses and the acquisition;

31
00:01:49,283 --> 00:01:52,480
every segment opens the
parameter behind it.

32
00:01:52,730 --> 00:01:55,887
The plan lists temperature,
field, sequence,

33
00:01:55,887 --> 00:02:00,542
scans and τ values for each
row, and estimates the run time.

34
00:02:00,792 --> 00:02:04,283
Settings records which
sequences the hardware has.

35
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:10,084
Run plan starts the experiment,
one row after another.

36
00:02:10,334 --> 00:02:15,155
Live acquisition shows every scan
as it arrives, with its spectrum.

37
00:02:15,405 --> 00:02:21,989
M is taken in the Mz window, with its σ,
the noise, and the signal-to-noise ratio.

38
00:02:22,239 --> 00:02:25,473
The average gets quieter
as the scans add up.

39
00:02:25,723 --> 00:02:30,144
M(τ) of the current field
builds up, point by point.

40
00:02:30,394 --> 00:02:34,619
The current field is fitted again
each time a new point arrives,

41
00:02:34,619 --> 00:02:38,118
with one, two or three
exponentials, in milliseconds;

42
00:02:38,118 --> 00:02:42,033
the fit is marked partial
until the field is complete.

43
00:02:42,283 --> 00:02:44,304
Meanwhile, Results follows the run:

44
00:02:44,304 --> 00:02:48,581
each finished field can be looked
at while the next one is measured.

45
00:02:50,231 --> 00:02:52,862
The noise analysis is your choice.

46
00:02:53,112 --> 00:02:55,610
The phase treatment can
be phase independent,

47
00:02:55,610 --> 00:02:56,942
two-phase or four-phase,

48
00:02:56,942 --> 00:02:59,844
with the noise from the
scatter between scans.

49
00:03:00,094 --> 00:03:04,329
The previous Prospa analysis
stays available, for comparison.

50
00:03:04,579 --> 00:03:09,224
A Gaussian filter can be previewed
on the last scan before it is saved:

51
00:03:09,224 --> 00:03:10,009
here 20 kHz,

52
00:03:10,009 --> 00:03:13,957
with the filtered and unfiltered
averages side by side.

53
00:03:14,207 --> 00:03:15,448
On the ultraRelax8,

54
00:03:15,448 --> 00:03:20,150
a short noise and health check is
compared with the machine's reference,

55
00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:22,851
value by value, and kept as a trend.

56
00:03:24,501 --> 00:03:28,235
The selected magnet defines
its diagnostic groups,

57
00:03:28,235 --> 00:03:32,542
channels and units. Here,
all readings are simulated.

58
00:03:32,792 --> 00:03:36,805
Temperature is followed as a
trend. The supply voltages are

59
00:03:36,805 --> 00:03:40,216
sampled at the start of
each actual plan row.

60
00:03:40,466 --> 00:03:43,955
Controller settings are
read-only when available. This

61
00:03:43,955 --> 00:03:47,342
simulator reports its
PID gains as unavailable.

62
00:03:47,592 --> 00:03:51,621
The diagnostic route can be
direct, through the magnet supply,

63
00:03:51,621 --> 00:03:57,040
or through the vendor console. Real
hardware drivers still need qualification.

64
00:03:57,290 --> 00:04:02,755
The Hall voltage is shown live, with the
console's field-switching pulses over it.

65
00:04:03,005 --> 00:04:05,961
Every switch is also
recorded at the full rate:

66
00:04:05,961 --> 00:04:09,105
here the last field-down
and field-up transitions,

67
00:04:09,105 --> 00:04:10,901
with the settling band.

68
00:04:11,151 --> 00:04:14,855
Each transition is measured:
delay, rise and fall time,

69
00:04:14,855 --> 00:04:17,615
overshoot, settling time and pulse width,

70
00:04:17,615 --> 00:04:20,052
as the last value and the mean.

71
00:04:20,302 --> 00:04:26,842
Transition times use the monitor's own
clock. Lost data is flagged, never hidden.

72
00:04:27,092 --> 00:04:30,571
Fixed field plus uSpin32
selects a different magnet

73
00:04:30,571 --> 00:04:34,605
definition. Unneeded
field-switching panels disappear.

74
00:04:36,255 --> 00:04:39,617
The final analysis is OneFit Engine's.

75
00:04:39,867 --> 00:04:42,885
Fit in OFE fits every field with OFE-Go,

76
00:04:42,885 --> 00:04:46,431
with MINOS errors and
reduced chi-square: here,

77
00:04:46,431 --> 00:04:48,441
four simulated fields.

78
00:04:48,691 --> 00:04:50,642
The T1 dispersion is plotted,

79
00:04:50,642 --> 00:04:54,691
together with the T1 that
Prospa wrote, for comparison.

80
00:04:54,941 --> 00:04:59,144
The models are full OFE
expressions, and can be edited.

81
00:05:00,794 --> 00:05:05,348
Open in OFE-GUI sends the
fit to a running OFE-GUI.

82
00:05:05,598 --> 00:05:09,009
It refits it and plots every
field, to change the model,

83
00:05:09,009 --> 00:05:11,187
the bounds or the plots there.

84
00:05:12,837 --> 00:05:17,850
The Terminal pane is a real shell
on the computer running OneNMRD,

85
00:05:17,850 --> 00:05:21,087
inside the page. It is off by default.

86
00:05:21,337 --> 00:05:25,808
Its Claude and Codex buttons start a
separately installed coding agent there,

87
00:05:25,808 --> 00:05:28,596
in a Docker sandbox when one is available.

88
00:05:28,846 --> 00:05:33,107
OneNMRD writes an AGENTS file
for them: how to reach the GUI,

89
00:05:33,107 --> 00:05:36,042
the hardware rules, and the JSON API.

90
00:05:36,292 --> 00:05:39,584
Here the API lists the
saved simulator run.

91
00:05:39,834 --> 00:05:43,739
A Tune or a Run asked for by an
agent waits for your Approve;

92
00:05:43,739 --> 00:05:45,562
Stop is always allowed.

93
00:05:47,212 --> 00:05:50,342
Plan, acquire, watch, and fit.

94
00:05:50,592 --> 00:05:54,661
OneNMRD Interface connects the
selected console and magnet,

95
00:05:54,661 --> 00:05:57,769
and hands the analysis to OneFit Engine.

96
00:05:58,019 --> 00:06:02,258
OneNMRD uses the Artistic
License 2.0. Public downloads

97
00:06:02,258 --> 00:06:05,572
include the applications
and runtime files;

98
00:06:05,572 --> 00:06:10,392
private application source and
Prospa macros are excluded.

99
00:06:10,642 --> 00:06:15,193
Prospa and uSpin32 remain
separate products. This tour used

100
00:06:15,193 --> 00:06:17,471
the simulator throughout.
